  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date the Department of Education has $1.9B in contract obligations across 610 awards, with an average award size of $3.2M. Obligations fell 22.2% year over year. That decline comes amid multi-year volatility: prior fiscal-year totals include $2.7B in FY21, $2.4B in FY22, $2.4B in FY23, $2.7B in FY24, and $2.5B in FY25, with FY26 at $1.9B. Spending in FY2026 to date is concentrated in a few large categories. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation accounts for $960M and Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $458M, together representing the majority of current-year obligations. Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities is $143M and several IT and financial services categories follow at smaller totals. Vendor concentration is also high. NELNET SERVICING LLC received $294M, MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC received $251M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $238M in FY2026 to date. The current picture is one of lower overall obligations, heavy weighting toward credit intermediation and IT services, and a short list of large prime contractors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 22.2% year over year. FY26 to date obligations are $1.9B versus $2.5B in FY25 and earlier fiscal years that ranged as high as $2.7B. That decline coincides with a shift of spending into a few large categories rather than broad-based increases across many NAICS codes. The current fiscal-year totals are partial, and FY26 is reported as fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Education’s contract spending concentrated?",
        "body": "Spending is concentrated in a small number of categories and vendors. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation is $960M and Computer Systems Design Services is $458M in FY2026 to date, together accounting for a large share of obligations. The top vendors are similarly concentrated, with NELNET SERVICING LLC at $294M, MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $251M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $238M."
      }
    ]
  },
